  "details": "1. Make an animation in Unity that changes the position and/or size of the contact sender/receiver. The contacts are disabled at first and become enabled at the end of the animation (after changing position/size).\n\n2. Try it in Unity and watch it work as expected.\n\n3. Upload avatar and try it in-game.\n\n4. Contacts won't move or change size after the first time they are enabled.\n\nMore info about my setup:\n\nMy avatar has a stick that transforms into differently shaped weapons. This stick moves from my back to my hand via constraints. The contact sender and receiver are in an empty object at the root of my avatar (totally separate from the item) and have the stick set as the transform source. The contacts are disabled by default and aren't enabled until I turn the stick into one of the weapons. The contacts will move and change shape ONCE the first time they are enabled. After this, they don't change at all.",
